# Experiment 1

## Aim

Design and implement a CI/CD pipeline for a Java application built using Maven. Use Git/GitHub for version control, Jenkins for pipeline execution, Docker for containerization, and deploy the application on Docker Swarm.

---

## Architecture

```text
Developer
    │
    ▼
GitHub
    │
    ▼
Jenkins
    │
    ▼
Maven Build
    │
    ▼
Docker Build
    │
    ▼
Docker Swarm
    │
    ▼
Running Service
```

---

## Steps

### 1. Create Project Folder

```bash
mkdir java-cicd-app
cd java-cicd-app
```

---

### 2. Create Maven Folder Structure

```bash
mkdir -p src/main/java/com/example
```

Project Structure:

```text
java-cicd-app
│── pom.xml
│── Dockerfile
│── Jenkinsfile
└── src
    └── main
        └── java
            └── com
                └── example
                    └── App.java
```

---

### 3. Create Java File

```bash
nano src/main/java/com/example/App.java
```

Paste the following code:

```java
package com.example;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("CI/CD Pipeline Running Successfully");
    }
}
```

Save the file:

```text
CTRL + O
Enter
CTRL + X
```

---

### 4. Create pom.xml

```bash
nano pom.xml
```

Paste:

```xml
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>java-cicd-app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0</version>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>
    </properties>
</project>
```

---

### 5. Build Maven Project

```bash
mvn clean package
```

Generated file:

```text
target/java-cicd-app-1.0.jar
```

---

### 6. Run Java Application

```bash
java -cp target/java-cicd-app-1.0.jar com.example.App
```

Output:

```text
CI/CD Pipeline Running Successfully
```

---

### 7. Create Dockerfile

```bash
nano Dockerfile
```

Paste:

```dockerfile
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/java-cicd-app-1.0.jar app.jar

CMD ["java","-cp","app.jar","com.example.App"]
```

---

### 8. Build Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t java-cicd-app:v1 .
```

---

### 9. Run Docker Container

```bash
docker run java-cicd-app:v1
```

Output:

```text
CI/CD Pipeline Running Successfully
```

---

### 10. Initialize Git

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial Commit"
```

---

### 11. Push Project to GitHub

```bash
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main
```

---

### 12. Initialize Docker Swarm

```bash
docker swarm init
```

---

### 13. Deploy Application on Docker Swarm

```bash
docker service create --name java-service --replicas 2 java-cicd-app:v1
```

---

### 14. Verify Service

```bash
docker service ls
```

---

### 15. Create Jenkinsfile

```bash
nano Jenkinsfile
```

Paste:

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }

        stage('Docker Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'docker build -t java-cicd-app:v1 .'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                sh 'docker service create --name java-service --replicas 2 java-cicd-app:v1'
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 16. Push Jenkinsfile to GitHub

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Added Jenkinsfile"
git push
```

---

### 17. Jenkins Execution Steps

1. Open Jenkins.
2. Click **New Item**.
3. Enter project name: **java-cicd-pipeline**.
4. Select **Pipeline**.
5. Click **OK**.
6. Under **Pipeline**, select **Pipeline script from SCM**.
7. Choose **Git**.
8. Enter the GitHub Repository URL.
9. Branch: **main**.
10. Script Path: **Jenkinsfile**.
11. Click **Save**.
12. Click **Build Now**.

---

## Result

The Java Maven application was successfully built using Maven, version-controlled with Git/GitHub, automated using Jenkins, containerized using Docker, and deployed successfully on Docker Swarm through a CI/CD pipeline.# Experiment 3

